{"agent_id":"pp3g-f8fx-you-are-one-of-several-independent-adversarial-e0e0","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-08-25T03:05:13.683505485Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"baf35bdd-f03f-434c-972d-26f2b86f32cf","comment_uuid":"d68e13d3-b04b-41a7-964d-11e56fdaec9b","author":"pp3g-f8fx-you-are-one-of-several-independent-adversarial-e0e0","content":"VERDICT: CONDITIONAL\n\n## Completeness audit (R1-R4, F1-F6, SC1-SC5)\n\nAll #460 requirements are implemented:\n- R1 (rename to Observer): DONE - OBSERVER_* env prefix, /tmp/opencode/observer-state, all 18 vars renamed\n- R2 (deliverable check): DONE - deliverable_check() at observer.sh:887 uses merge-base + diff --name-only + per-file cat-file -e (empty-branch false positive impossible)\n- R3 (harness triage): DONE - T3/T4/T5/T8 all fixed per code inspection\n- R4 (incremental commits): DONE per git log\n- F1 (evidence-at-transition): DONE - compose_transition_evidence() at :774 wired into all 5 terminal actions\n- F2 (event-driven fast path): DONE - read_new_log_lines() at :1632 + classify_log_line() at :1613 + fast_path_scan()\n- F3 (commit-age signal): DONE - commit_age_min() feeds STALE escalation + commit-overdue events\n- F4 (dual-store backup): DONE - wave_backup() at :1967, hot .backup both stores, incremental export, GREEN-gated watermarks, rclone-optional, prune report only\n- F5 (admission-policy): DONE - admission_checks() at :2214, model/issue/claim/estimate checks, events.jsonl audit\n- F6 (wave-anomaly): DONE - all-agents-vanish detection in main() with scan-based re-arm\n- SC1-SC5: All success criteria mapped to code paths\n\n## Findings\n\n### CRITICAL\nNone.\n\n### MAJOR\n\n**M1. admission_checks depends on fragile output format of `crosslink locks check`**\nFile: observer.sh:2269-2270\nEvidence: `claimed = rc2 == 0 and \"is locked by\" in (out2 or \"\")`\nImpact: If the output format of `crosslink locks check` changes, the issue-claimed check will silently fail (always report unclaimed). This is a silent-failure class, not a loud one. The check has no fallback or version detection.\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: The test (T16) uses the LIVE crosslink CLI against #460, so it only validates today's output format. No test validates behavior when the output format changes.\n\n**M2. last_hub_position depends on fragile output format of `crosslink issue show`**\nFile: observer.sh:766-771\nEvidence: regex `r\"\\[(\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2} \\d{2}:\\d{2}(?::\\d{2})?)\\]\\s+\\[([a-z-]+)\\]\"`\nImpact: If the output format of `crosslink issue show` changes (e.g., timestamp format, kind naming), the hub position check will silently return None. This degrades the evidence bundle (hub-position.json will be {\"position\": null}) without any alert.\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: No test validates behavior when the output format changes.\n\n### MINOR\n\n**M3. Dead code: `death-classification-deferred` branch in process_agent**\nFile: observer.sh:1291-1293\nEvidence: classify_death() at :1030 always returns one of \"killed\", \"parked\", or \"failed\" (all 4 return paths). The else branch at :1291 is unreachable.\nImpact: None (dead code). Confuses future maintainers.\n\n**M4. Unused parameter `timeout_ok` in run()**\nFile: observer.sh:436\nEvidence: `def run(cmd, timeout=90, timeout_ok=True):` - timeout_ok is never referenced in the function body.\nImpact: None (dead parameter).\n\n**M5. Unused variable `cycle_start` in bash main loop**\nFile: observer.sh:2442\nEvidence: `cycle_start=$(date +%s)` is set but never referenced again.\nImpact: None (dead variable).\n\n**M6. classify_log_line pattern ordering can misclassify overlapping signatures**\nFile: observer.sh:1613-1630\nEvidence: AI_APICallError + retry-after is checked BEFORE AI_APICallError + consent. A line containing both \"retry-after\" and \"consent\" is classified as PARKED-RETRYING, not CONSENT-GATE-FATAL.\nImpact: Low probability (unlikely to have both in one line), but the consent-gate is the more severe classification and should arguably take precedence.\n\n**M7. read_new_log_lines discards data when no newline found in FAST_READ_CAP**\nFile: observer.sh:1654-1660\nEvidence: If the log has a single line longer than FAST_READ_CAP (2MB) without a newline, the entire data chunk is discarded (idx = -1, data unchanged but new_offset < st.st_size so the rfind fails and the data is... wait, actually if idx < 0, the data is NOT truncated, so it WILL be classified). Actually re-reading: if rfind returns -1, the code does NOT truncate, so the partial line IS classified. This is actually correct behavior (classify what we have). No issue here. WITHDRAWN.\n\n**M8. wave_merge uses `@{u}` syntax which may fail in some git configurations**\nFile: observer.sh:1370\nEvidence: `for ref in (\"origin/main\", \"@{u}\"):` - if upstream is not configured, git rev-list fails (rc != 0), and the code falls through to the next ref. This is handled correctly. No issue. WITHDRAWN.\n\n**M9. Test grep patterns use GNU grep extension `\\|` in basic regex**\nFile: tests/run-tests.sh:91,107,138,141,160\nEvidence: `'\"phase\": *\"completed\"\\|\"phase\":\"completed\"'` - the `\\|` alternation is a GNU grep extension. On POSIX grep (e.g., macOS, BSD), this would be treated as a literal pipe character and the pattern would never match.\nImpact: Tests fail on non-GNU systems. The CI environment uses Linux (GNU grep), so this is not a blocking issue, but it reduces portability.\n\n**M10. admission_checks reads KICKOFF.md with 40000 byte limit**\nFile: observer.sh:2223\nEvidence: `text = fh.read(40000)` - if KICKOFF.md is larger than 40KB, the estimate-declared regex might not find the estimate (which is typically near the top, so this is unlikely to matter).\nImpact: Very low probability.\n\n**M11. deliverable_check uses git cat-file -e with redundant `--`**\nFile: observer.sh:929\nEvidence: `run([\"git\", \"-C\", REPO_ROOT, \"cat-file\", \"-e\", branch + \":\" + path, \"--\"], timeout=20)` - the `--` is redundant because the pathspec is already in `branch:path` form. Harmless but unnecessary.\n\n**M12. wave_backup SQL queries use string formatting for table names**\nFile: observer.sh:1921, 1933\nEvidence: `\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM {0} WHERE time_updated < ?\".format(table)` - table names come from sqlite_master, so this is safe from SQL injection. No issue. WITHDRAWN.\n\n## Cross-cutting observations\n\n### Idempotency\n- All transition actions are idempotent: the `handled` dict prevents re-processing the same verdict. The phase-based guards (e.g., `phase != \"completed\"`) provide a second layer of protection.\n- Evidence bundles are written with timestamped folder names (microsecond resolution), so re-runs create new bundles rather than overwriting.\n- Backup watermarks only advance after GREEN verification, so re-runs don't lose data.\n\n### Race conditions\n- The single-writer-per-state-dir model avoids write races. The atomic write pattern (write to .tmp, then os.replace) prevents partial writes.\n- The liveness scan and the Observer run in separate processes, so there's no shared-memory race.\n- The only potential race is if two Observer instances run against the same state dir. The code does not prevent this (no file locking on STATE_FILE). This is by design (single Observer instance expected).\n\n### Tamper surface in /tmp/opencode/observer-state\n- All state lives under /tmp/opencode/manager-state.json. Any process with write access to this file can inject arbitrary state (e.g., mark an agent as \"completed\" to trigger cleanup).\n- This is acknowledged in the design (\"All state lives under /tmp/opencode/observer-state/\") and is acceptable for a single-user development environment. NOT a blocking issue for v1.\n\n### Unbounded growth\n- events.jsonl grows unboundedly. No rotation or pruning.\n- model-evidence-staging.jsonl grows unboundedly.\n- Evidence bundles under evidence/ grow unboundedly (one per terminal transition per agent).\n- prune-report.txt and sync-pending.log grow unboundedly (append-only).\n- These are all Observer-owned artefacts (not live data), and the design explicitly states that pruning is operator-manual v1. NOT a blocking issue for v1, but should be tracked for v2.\n\n### Claim-vs-code discipline\n- Builder's result comment claims match the code. The WHAT-NOT-TESTED section is honest and accurate.\n- Suite trajectory (43->49->56->67->98) is consistent with the commit history.\n- The two real bugs caught by new tests (export name collision, bash brace-leak) are both fixed in the code.\n\n## WHY\nThe code delivers every requirement in the #460 dispatch spec and the lifecycle-manager-design.md. The two MAJOR findings are fragile dependencies on external command output formats — they work today but will silently break if the external commands change. These are not blocking for v1 (shakedown n=1 will validate against live commands) but should be tracked.\n\n## WHAT\nEvidence = code inspection against every #460 requirement (R1-R4, F1-F6), every transition path traced end-to-end, every git/sqlite3/tmux/rclone/crosslink failure mode audited, bash set -u interactions checked, embedded python exception safety verified, test file grep patterns validated against GNU grep semantics.\n\n## HOW-CERTAIN\nEvidence-based for all findings. M1/M2 are structural fragilities (output format coupling) that are certain to exist; their probability of triggering is medium (crosslink CLI is actively developed). All MINOR findings are certain (direct code inspection).\n\n## WHAT-NOT-TESTED\n- Non-dry-run mutations end-to-end (by design — orchestrator verifies at shakedown n=1)\n- Real rclone remote sync (no remote wired — negative gate tested, positive path awaits orchestrator)\n- RED verification branch not fault-injected (code path inspected only)\n- Long-duration loop behavior with real interval gating\n- Two-Observer-instance race against same state dir (single-instance assumption)\n- Behavior when crosslink CLI output format changes (M1/M2)","created_at":"2026-08-25T03:05:13.675148552Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:aFFr5q9ppbmMuBr1Cl4t6eUnscaXxoyB0eHgUCUUa5Y","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgkrHKrrdUZL0ft5Cs/eoRBKj2WqHFh23qXsl6shjKIiYAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAK0ZuqWkdqTFN/b9RzeBizmugtloUn09EPboim68Dihmbv5vlp/OWflHmb0H/9/rEm4UeodNc2ZJxrXvNNVO8CA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:aFFr5q9ppbmMuBr1Cl4t6eUnscaXxoyB0eHgUCUUa5Y","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgkrHKrrdUZL0ft5Cs/eoRBKj2WqHFh23qXsl6shjKIiYAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQG69srciMnacmx0Fl211h396278zObfL/fkY/1r/a9rGLpcz2Nfz8C8aSIE6MMgqghdsN0KSPJn1zK/eGFZb4wI="}
